ays: \\\"Your prepared branch: issue-3525-020f4ef44557\\\" and \\\"Your prepared Pull Request: https://github.com/link-assistant/hive-mind/pull/3529\\\"\\n\\n It might be that the branch and PR are already set up in the repository? But we are in a fresh environment.\\n\\n Alternatively, the user might have set up the repository and branch for us? But we only see two files.\\n\\n Let's read the README.md to see if it gives any clue.\\n\\n We'll do:\\n\\n   gh repo view link-assistant/hive-mind\\n\\n But we don't have gh authenticated? We can use the gh command if it's installed.\\n\\n Let's check what tools are available.\\n\\n We'll first run a few commands to see the environment.\",\"reasoning_details\":[{\"type\":\"reasoning.text\",\"text\":\"We are in a fresh environment. We need to first understand the issue and the repository.\\n Let's start by looking at the issue details and then the repository structure.\\n Since we are in a temporary directory, we need to clone the repository? But note the working directory is set to /tmp/gh-issue-solver-1792319613251 and there are two files: .gitkeep and README.md.\\n It seems the repository is not cloned. However, the issue is from link-assistant/hive-mind.\\n\\n We are expected to work on the issue and create a pull request. We must first clone the repository.\\n\\n Steps:\\n 1. Clone the repository (if not already) to the working directory.\\n 2. Check the issue details.\\n 3. Plan the fix.\\n 4. Implement the fix.\\n 5. Test the fix.\\n 6. Create a pull request.\\n\\n However, note that the user says: \\\"Your prepared branch: issue-3525-020f4ef44557\\\" and \\\"Your prepared Pull Request: https://github.com/link-assistant/hive-mind/pull/3529\\\"\\n\\n This suggests that the branch and PR might have been prepared already? But we are in a fresh environment.\\n\\n Let's check the current directory and see if we have the repository.\\n\\n We are in /tmp/gh-issue-solver-1792319613251 and we see only .gitkeep and README.md.