[2026-10-18T10:35:58.539Z] [INFO]             "text": "Now we have created the workflow. However, note that the action `scala/setup-scala@v1` might not exist. Let's check.\n\n We can use the official Scala setup by coursier or use sdkman. Alternatively, we can install Scala via coursier.\n\n Let's change the setup to use coursier, which is the recommended way.\n\n We'll do:\n   - Setup JDK\n   - Install coursier\n   - Use coursier to install Scala\n\n Alternatively, we can use the action from the Scala GitHub organization: `scala/setup-scala` does exist? Let's check by searching.\n\n But to be safe, we can use a step that installs Scala via coursier.\n\n Let's update the workflow to use coursier.\n\n We'll change the Scala setup step to:\n\n      - name: Install coursier\n        run: |\n          curl -fL https://github.com/coursier/launchers/raw/master/cs-x86_64-pc-linux.gz | gzip -d > cs\n          chmod +x cs\n          ./cs setup\n\n      - name: Install Scala\n        run: |\n          ./cs install scala:3.3.1\n          echo \"$HOME/.local/share/coursier/bin\" >> $GITHUB_PATH\n\n However, note that the workflow runs on ubuntu-latest and we can also use the setup-scala action if it exists.\n\n Let's first check if the action exists by trying to use it in a test? But we can also look for it.\n\n Alternatively, we can use the following (which is common in Scala projects):\n\n      - name: Setup Scala\n        uses: scala/setup-scala@v1\n        with:\n          scala-version: '3.3.1'\n\n I think this action exists. Let's assume it does. If it fails, we can adjust.\n\n We'll keep it as is for now and test later.\n\n Now, let's update the todo list to mark the workflow creation as completed and move to testing.",
