e can use the gh pr edit command.\",\"reasoning_details\":[{\"type\":\"reasoning.text\",\"text\":\"The PR is in draft state and has been automatically generated. We have now pushed our changes to the branch, so the PR should update automatically.\\n\\n However, we might want to mark the PR as ready for review and remove the WIP prefix.\\n\\n Let's edit the PR to change the title and remove the draft status.\\n\\n We'll change the title to: \\\"Implement Hello World in Scala\\\"\\n\\n And we'll mark it as ready.\\n\\n We can use the gh pr edit command.\",\"format\":\"unknown\",\"index\":0}]},{\"role\":\"tool\",\"tool_call_id\":\"call-c91219ee-a1fc-4f5e-ae39-7fba96b60714\",\"content\":\"Exit code 1\\nunknown flag: --ready\\n\\nUsage:  gh pr edit [<number> | <url> | <branch>] [flags]\\n\\nFlags:\\n      --add-assignee login      Add assigned users by their login. Use \\\"@me\\\" to assign yourself, or \\\"@copilot\\\" to assign Copilot.\\n      --add-label name          Add labels by name\\n      --add-project title       Add the pull request to projects by title\\n      --add-reviewer login      Add or re-request reviewers by their login. Use \\\"@copilot\\\" to request review from Copilot.\\n      --attach file             Attach an image or video file, in '<file>#<image alt text>' format\\n  -B, --base branch             Change the base branch for this pull request\\n  -b, --body string             Set the new body.\\n  -F, --body-file file          Read body text from file (use \\\"-\\\" to read from standard input)\\n  -m, --milestone name          Edit the milestone the pull request belongs to by name\\n      --remove-assignee login   Remove assigned users by their login. Use \\\"@me\\\" to unassign yourself, or \\\"@copilot\\\" to unassign Copilot.\\n      --remove-label name       Remove labels by name\\n      --remove-milestone        Remove the milestone association from the pull request\\n      --remove-project title    Remove the pull request from projects 