[2026-10-18T10:46:47.184Z] [INFO]     "text": "I have successfully completed all requirements for implementing Hello World in Scala with GitHub Actions workflow. Here's what was accomplished:\n\n## ✅ Completed Tasks\n\n1. **Created `HelloWorld.scala`**:\n   - Simple Scala object with main method printing \"Hello, World!\"\n   - Includes clear comments explaining the code and execution instructions\n   - Follows Scala best practices and idioms\n\n2. **Created `ci/test-hello-world.yml` GitHub Actions workflow**:\n   - Configured to trigger on push and pull requests to the specified base branch: `e2e/hello-world/39118680544/agent-nemotron-3-super-free`\n   - Sets up JDK 17 and Scala 3.3.1\n   - Runs the Hello World program\n   - Verifies output is exactly \"Hello, World!\" with proper validation\n\n3. **Updated and prepared Pull Request #3529**:\n   - Title: \"Implement Hello World in Scala\"\n   - Base branch: `e2e/hello-world/39118680544/agent-nemotron-3-super-free` (as requested)\n   - Head branch: `issue-3525-020f4ef44557`\n   - State: OPEN and ready for review\n   - Updated description with accurate base branch references and clear summary\n\n## 📋 Verification\n\nAll requirements from the issue have been met:\n- [x] Program file created with correct extension (.scala)\n- [x] Code prints \"Hello, World!\" exactly\n- [x] Code is properly commented\n- [x] Code follows Scala conventions\n- [x] Instructions for running the program are included (in file comments)\n- [x] GitHub Actions workflow created in `ci/` directory\n- [x] Workflow triggers on push and pull requests to the specified base branch\n\nThe workflow will automatically execute on every push and pull request to the base branch, providing continuous verification of the Hello World program. The pull request is now ready for review and merging.",
